---
import { currentCourseProfile } from '@amat19/course-content'; import AppLayout from '../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
---
<AppLayout title="Course map"><section class="page-width page-intro"><h1 class="display-title">One finite-math path, five connected modules.</h1><p class="page-context">Current semester course map</p><p class="lede">The current AY 2025–2026 course guide is the scope authority. Older handout-only topics are labeled supplemental instead of silently treated as current requirements.</p></section><section class="page-width module-section"><div class="course-roadmap">{currentCourseProfile.modules.map((module,index)=><article class="roadmap-module"><span class="roadmap-module__number">0{index+1}</span><div><h2><a href={module.href}>{module.title}</a></h2><p>{module.description}</p><div class="roadmap-skills">{currentCourseProfile.skills.filter(s=>s.module===module.id).map(skill=><a href={skill.relatedLab||module.href}><span class="status-pill">{skill.status}</span>{skill.title}</a>)}</div></div></article>)}</div></section><section class="page-width module-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><h2>After the module labs</h2><p class="section-context">Whole-course practice</p></div></div><div class="route-grid"><a class="route-link" href="/practice"><span><strong>Mixed Practice</strong><small>Immediate feedback across the implemented core modules.</small></span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="route-link" href="/exam"><span><strong>Mixed Course Check</strong><small>Original generated set with feedback held until submission.</small></span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="route-link" href="/reference"><span><strong>Formula & Notation Reference</strong><small>Compact formulas with assumptions and links back to the live tools.</small></span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="route-link" href="/progress"><span><strong>Progress & Local Data</strong><small>Review transparent skill evidence and export your browser-local study data.</small></span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section><section class="page-width feature-band"><div><h2>Current guide first; older depth stays visible but labeled.</h2><p class="section-context">Scope policy</p></div><div class="feature-band__grid"><p><strong>Current core:</strong> Logic, Probability, Financial Mathematics, Matrices, Linear Programming and Game Theory.</p><p><strong>Supplemental:</strong> older-material topics such as expected value/variance, simplex and Markov chains remain useful but are visibly marked.</p><p><strong>Public content:</strong> examples are original. Uploaded handouts and exams are used for terminology, scope and assessment patterns—not republished as a question bank.</p></div></section></AppLayout>
